write_node(t, ind) -> str — serializes one node to indented JSON, recursing into children
example: {"id": "F01", "layer": 2, "text": "…", "lines": […], "children": [
  {"id": "F01.1", …}
]}

write_map(path, m) -> None — serializes m to path as a single JSON object
example: {"file": "x.py", "links": […], "terms": […], "map": [
    {"id": "F01", "layer": 1, "text": "…", "lines": […], "children": […]}
  ]}

